# Two small computations: line and quadratic fits to 40 noisy points, and a Monte Carlo estimate of pi

## 1. Straight-line fit to 40 noisy points

Data: x = 0, 1, ..., 39; y = 2.5 + 0.8 x + e, with e ~ N(0, 3^2) drawn as `rng.normal(0, 3, size=40)` after `numpy.random.default_rng(227)`. Ordinary least squares; 95% confidence intervals are t-intervals with df = 38 (t = 2.0244).

| parameter | estimate | std. error | 95% CI | generating value |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| slope | 0.7484 | 0.0387 | [0.6701, 0.8267] | 0.8 |
| intercept | 3.9447 | 0.8769 | [2.1696, 5.7198] | 2.5 |

R^2 = 0.908, residual SD = 2.825 (generating SD 3). Both CIs contain the generating values.

### 1b. Quadratic fit and comparison with the line (AIC)

Same 40 points (`results/data.csv`), model y = a + b x + c x^2 fitted by OLS; 95% CIs are t-intervals with df = 37 (t = 2.0262). The generating model has c = 0.

| parameter | estimate | std. error | 95% CI | generating value |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| a | 4.9716 | 1.2718 | [2.3947, 7.5484] | 2.5 |
| b | 0.5863 | 0.1509 | [0.2806, 0.8919] | 0.8 |
| c | 0.00416 | 0.00374 | [-0.00342, 0.01173] | 0 |

Residual SD = 2.816, R^2 = 0.911 (line: 2.825, 0.908). The CI for c contains 0 (p = 0.273, equivalent F-test for c = 0: F = 1.236); the CIs for a and b contain the generating values. a, b and c are strongly correlated (covariance matrix in `results/fit_quadratic.json`, `cov_abc`), so the shift of a and b relative to the line fit is not independent evidence of anything.

AIC = 2k - 2 log L with the Gaussian log-likelihood at the MLE variance RSS/n and k = number of coefficients + 1 (the error variance); the same constant enters both models, so differences are exact.

| model | k | RSS | AIC | AICc | Akaike weight (AIC) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| line | 3 | 303.27 | 200.55 | 201.21 | 0.585 |
| quadratic | 4 | 293.47 | 201.23 | 202.37 | 0.415 |

**Which model the data support:** the straight line, but only mildly. AIC(quadratic) - AIC(line) = 0.69 (AICc: 1.16), i.e. the line is preferred by less than 2 AIC units, the usual threshold for a meaningful difference. The extra parameter lowers RSS by only 3.2% (303.3 to 293.5), which does not pay for the penalty of 2 AIC units. Together with the CI of c including 0, this gives no support for curvature; it is not strong evidence either way, and the data are consistent with the true (linear) generating model.

