## 2. Monte Carlo estimate of pi (`simulate.py`)

`code/simulate.py` (the unmodified script supplied in the initial state) was run once in full as `python3 -u simulate.py --out results.json`: 90 chunks x 60,000,000 points, chunk i seeded `random.Random(227+i)`, wall time 750.5 s. The estimate is the mean of the 90 chunk estimates; the interval it prints is mean +/- 1.96 * sd / sqrt(90) (normal quantile).

| quantity | value |
|---|---|
| estimate of pi | 3.1415628 |
| printed 95% interval | [3.1415193, 3.1416063] |
| pi = 3.14159265... inside the interval? | **yes** |

The full printed log is `results/simulate.log`; the numbers are in `results/results.json`. `results/simulate_partial_aborted.log` is an abandoned earlier attempt (67 of 90 chunks) and is not used anywhere in this report.

